WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.559
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:09.269
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:18.038
Unit five: Modal Verbs: Can, Must, Should and Have To. Today you will talk about ability, rules, advice and obligation.

4
00:00:18.338 --> 00:00:20.909
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:24.949
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.783 --> 00:00:26.633
Ability.

7
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.079
Ability means being able to do something.

8
00:00:30.683 --> 00:00:32.253
Swimming is an ability.

9
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.363
Your turn. Say: Ability.

10
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.224
Ability.

11
00:00:39.983 --> 00:00:40.880
Permission.

12
00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:44.487
Permission means allowing someone to do something.

13
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:46.560
Ask for permission.

14
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.802
Your turn. Say: Permission.

15
00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:53.552
Permission.

16
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:55.178
Advice.

17
00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:59.054
Advice means an idea about what someone should do.

18
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:01.162
Give her some advice.

19
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.518
Your turn. Say: Advice.

20
00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.565
Advice.

21
00:01:09.317 --> 00:01:10.469
Obligation.

22
00:01:11.483 --> 00:01:13.901
Obligation means something you must do.

23
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:16.203
Homework is an obligation.

24
00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:19.504
Your turn. Say: Obligation.

25
00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:23.495
Obligation.

26
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.274
Prohibition.

27
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:28.817
Prohibition means a rule that says you must not.

28
00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:30.952
Smoking is a prohibition.

29
00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.202
Your turn. Say: Prohibition.

30
00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.056
Prohibition.

31
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:39.911
Necessary.

32
00:01:40.917 --> 00:01:42.603
Necessary means needed.

33
00:01:43.217 --> 00:01:45.344
It is necessary to wear a helmet.

34
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:49.090
Your turn. Say: Necessary.

35
00:01:51.933 --> 00:01:53.143
Necessary.

36
00:01:53.883 --> 00:01:54.768
Rule.

37
00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:58.387
Rule means something you must follow.

38
00:01:58.983 --> 00:02:00.611
Follow the school rules.

39
00:02:01.217 --> 00:02:03.474
Your turn. Say: Rule.

40
00:02:06.333 --> 00:02:07.172
Rule.

41
00:02:07.917 --> 00:02:08.767
Helmet.

42
00:02:09.783 --> 00:02:12.085
Helmet means a hard hat for safety.

43
00:02:12.683 --> 00:02:13.801
Wear a helmet.

44
00:02:14.417 --> 00:02:16.756
Your turn. Say: Helmet.

45
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.485
Helmet.

46
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.206
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:28.259
Visal, what do modal verbs do?

48
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:45.473
Modal verbs such as can, must and should come before the base verb. They show ability, rules, advice and obligation. They have no -s in the third person, so we say she can swim, not she cans swim.

49
00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:49.256
What is the difference between must and have to?

50
00:02:50.350 --> 00:03:05.671
Must is often a strong personal feeling, for example, I must study harder. Have to is for rules and outside obligation, such as Students have to wear uniforms. Must not means it is forbidden.

51
00:03:06.783 --> 00:03:08.295
How do we give advice?

52
00:03:09.383 --> 00:03:14.567
We use should and shouldn't: You should drink more water. You shouldn't stay up late.

53
00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.177
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:18.017 --> 00:03:20.875
Grammar focus: Modal plus base verb.

55
00:03:21.175 --> 00:03:22.339
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.655
She can swim very well.

57
00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:28.176
Students must not use phones in class.

58
00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:36.221
Modal verbs are followed by the base verb. Use should for advice, must or have to for obligation and must not for prohibition.

59
00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:40.483
Be careful! Don't say: She cans swim very well.

60
00:03:42.433 --> 00:03:44.746
Say: She can swim very well.

61
00:03:45.046 --> 00:03:46.628
No -s after a modal.

62
00:03:47.433 --> 00:03:50.109
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.098
School Rules.

64
00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.967
Students must arrive before seven o'clock.

65
00:03:55.967 --> 00:03:58.187
They have to wear a uniform every day.

66
00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.467
They must not use phones in class.

67
00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:06.301
A teacher says students should ask questions when they do not understand.

68
00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:10.077
Everyone can use the library after lessons.

69
00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:14.971
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:15.817 --> 00:04:17.526
She blank swim very well.

71
00:04:17.826 --> 00:04:21.445
A, cans. B, is can. C, can.

72
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.744
The answer is C: can.

73
00:04:27.883 --> 00:04:30.838
You blank drink more water. It is good advice.

74
00:04:31.138 --> 00:04:34.617
A, should. B, must not. C, can.

75
00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:39.911
The answer is A: should.

76
00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:44.596
Students blank use phones in class. It is forbidden.

77
00:04:44.896 --> 00:04:48.561
A, can. B, must not. C, should.

78
00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:54.668
The answer is B: must not.

79
00:04:55.817 --> 00:04:56.911
Which is correct?

80
00:04:57.211 --> 00:05:01.340
A, She cans sing.. B, She can to sing.. C, She can sing..

81
00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.178
The answer is C: She can sing..

82
00:05:08.317 --> 00:05:10.142
Students have to wear blank.

83
00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:15.164
A, a uniform. B, pyjamas. C, a helmet only.

84
00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:20.700
The answer is A: a uniform.

85
00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.808
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:27.429
What are some rules at your school?

87
00:05:36.217 --> 00:05:37.787
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:38.087 --> 00:05:51.144
At my school we must arrive before seven o'clock and we have to wear a uniform. We must not use phones in class. We should respect our teachers, and we can use the library after lessons.

89
00:05:51.444 --> 00:05:53.107
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:54.017 --> 00:05:58.457
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and modal plus base verb.

91
00:05:58.757 --> 00:06:02.268
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

92
00:06:02.568 --> 00:06:04.942
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

93
00:06:05.242 --> 00:06:08.092
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

